# mw-release: the middleware release signing key (public half only).
#
# Algorithm   ECDSA P-256 / SHA-256 (devices verify raw r||s, 64 bytes)
# Held in     TPM 2.0 (Infineon SLB9672, firmware 15.24) of the release
#             workstation, via tpm2-pkcs11, token "mw", label "mw-release".
#             Generated inside the TPM on 2026-11-16; not extractable.
#             No other copy of the private key exists: if that TPM is
#             cleared or lost, devices claimed to this key must be
#             re-claimed by hand (BOOT-button re-key window, or a USB/SWD
#             reflash of the trust record).
# Sign with   mwctl --pkcs11 mw-release ...   (PKCS11_MODULE, PKCS11_TOKEN,
#             PKCS11_PIN from the environment or ~/.env; needs group tss)
# Pin with    mwctl --port <PORT> trust claim --pkcs11 mw-release
#
# Device wire form (sys/trust/claim body, compressed SEC1, 33 bytes):
02fd50725bc57d9d6db78985f1844bd067a2d71b647d1342329295dfadd37c654a
#
# SHA-256 of the DER SubjectPublicKeyInfo:
# a0f5200636852bb0da568ba398e7325686725cc3698fadcc214f18bd65ded45d
#
-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----
MFkwEwYHKoZIzj0CAQYIKoZIzj0DAQcDQgAE/VByW8V9nW23iYXxhEvQZ6LXG2R9
E0IykpXfrdN8ZUqxwuZ6S8OhyS70J7gTsIBLUtUyYqTFb1wFHje45WNhbA==
-----END PUBLIC KEY-----
